    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3513\n\nSPONSOR: GRIFFO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize Douglas Brenning of the village of New York Mills to\ntake the competitive civil service examination for the position of\npolice officer and be placed on the eligible list for employment as a\nfull-time police officer for the village of New York Mills police\ndepartment\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would grant a waiver to Douglas Brenning to take the compet-\nitive civil service examination for the position of police officer in\nthe village of New York Mills.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 allows for Douglas Brenning to take the competitive civil\nservice examination for the position of police officer in the Village of\nNew York Mills.\n\nSection 2 stipulates that Douglas Brenning shall be subject to the merit\nand fitness provisions of the civil service law.\n\nSection 3 marks the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDouglas Brenning, a part-time police officer, has been granted by the\nmayor and police chief of the Village of New York Mills the opportunity\nto seek an age-based waiver to take the competitive examination to\nbecome a full-time officer with the village's police department. This\nlegislation would provide Officer Brenning with the opportunity to test\nfor the full-time position, as approved by the mayor and chief of the\nvillage.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
